# Citation metadata for pretium, in Citation File Format 1.2.0.
# https://citation-file-format.github.io/
#
# NO DOI YET. A DOI is deliberately absent rather than invented: the fields
# `doi:` and `identifiers:` are left out until the repository is deposited to
# Zenodo, which mints one per release and one concept DOI for the project as a
# whole. That deposit is the next step for citability, and when it happens the
# `doi:` field and a `date-released:` for the tagged version belong here.
#
# `version:` tracks the `version` field in pyproject.toml. `date-released:` is
# omitted because nothing has been tagged or released yet, and a plausible date
# for a release that did not happen is worse than no date.
#
# A citation identifies the software. It does not identify a RUN. Reproducing a
# published result needs the seed, the universe fingerprint, the model preset
# name and the order log as well; see docs/reproducing-a-run.md.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: pretium
abstract: >-
  A deterministic market simulator with a real limit order book. A Rust core
  with a Python API. The same seed produces the same market on every platform,
  every price move carries a labelled factor decomposition, and orders match
  against depth so trading moves the price.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Coombes
    given-names: Simon
    email: simon@coombes.io
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/simoncoombes/pretium"
url: "https://simoncoombes.github.io/pretium/"
keywords:
  - market simulation
  - limit order book
  - deterministic simulation
  - agent-based finance
  - reproducible research
  - transaction cost analysis
